<title>USA: MBIA qualifies five muni bond issues for insurance.</title>
<headline>MBIA qualifies five muni bond issues for insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>MBIA Insurance Corp said Wednesday it qualified for bond insurance the following five municipal issues scheduled for competitive sale today:</p>
<p>--Corona Redevelopment Agency, Calif., $9.64 million tax allocation bonds, by direct purchase.</p>
<p>--La Porte, Ind., $2.735 million GOs</p>
<p>--Eaton County, Mich., $2.295 million water supply and sewerage district bonds.</p>
<p>--Salem, Ore., $6 million general obligation bonds.</p>
<p>--Mont Belvieu, Texas, $12 million GOs.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
